Expose the complex constructors in full Darwin C mode.

Source: Libm-2026 (17a5f9daa3f5679f7536b26f133b40cc078753c3), Source/complex.h after complex.patch.
Scope: macOS SDK 26.5, arm64 and x86_64.

The 26.5 comparison exposes these macros in full Darwin modes before C11,
while strict C99 and restricted POSIX modes hide them. Use the public Darwin
namespace level from XNU sys/cdefs.h. The existing builtin bodies are retained.

Evidence: .agents/skills/review-macos-c-sdk/scripts/sdk_review/headers/data/macosx26.5/tested-header-repairs.md
records visibility checks across both targets and C dialects.

--- a/usr/include/complex.h
+++ b/usr/include/complex.h
@@ -40,8 +40,9 @@
 #define I _Complex_I
 
 /* C11 complex constructors, ISO/IEC 9899 7.3.9.3. */
-#if !defined(__cplusplus) && defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 201112L \
-    && __has_builtin(__builtin_complex)
+#if !defined(__cplusplus) && __has_builtin(__builtin_complex) && \
+    ((defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 201112L) || \
+     __DARWIN_C_LEVEL >= __DARWIN_C_FULL)
 #define CMPLX(x, y)  __builtin_complex((double)(x), (double)(y))
 #define CMPLXF(x, y) __builtin_complex((float)(x), (float)(y))
 #define CMPLXL(x, y) __builtin_complex((long double)(x), (long double)(y))
